cokernel(ZZdFactorizationMap) -- make the cokernel of a map of ZZ/d-graded factorizations
*****************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note cokernel: (Macaulay2Doc)cokernel,
  * Usage: 
        cokernel f
        coker f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note map of ZZ/d-graded factorizations: ZZdFactorizationMap,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ZZ/d graded factorization: ZZdFactorization,, 

Description
===========

If $f : C \to D$ is a map of ZZ/d-graded factorizations of degree $d$, then the
cokernel is the factorization $E$ whose $i-th$ term is $cokernel(f_{i-d})$, and
whose differential is induced from the differential on the target.

In the following example, we first construct a random factorization morphism $f
: C \to D$.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
