collapseMF -- Converts a d-fold factorization into a (d-1)-fold factorization by composing the kth differential with the (k+1)th differential
*********************************************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        collapseMF(ZZdFactorization, ZZ)
  * Inputs:
      * ZZdFactorization, a *note ZZ/d graded factorization: ZZdFactorization,,
        A ZZdFactorization object representing a d-fold factorization
      * ZZ, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, An integer representing the
        kth differential
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ZZ/d graded factorization: ZZdFactorization,, 

Description
===========

This method collapses a d-fold factorization into a d-1-fold factorization by
composing the kth differential with the (k+1)th differential. It then permutes
