degree(ZZdFactorizationMap) -- get the degree of a map of ZZ/d-graded factorizations
************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note degree: (Macaulay2Doc)degree,
  * Usage: 
        degree f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note map of ZZ/d-graded factorizations: ZZdFactorizationMap,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 

Description
===========

A ZZ/d-graded factorization map $f : C \to D$ of degree $d$ is a sequence of of
maps $f_i : C_i \to D_{i+d}$. This method returns $d$.

The degree of the differential of a factorization is always -1.

