  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note ZZ/d graded factorization: ZZdFactorization,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note map of ZZ/d-graded factorizations: ZZdFactorizationMap,, a map
        of degree -1

A Z/d-graded factorization is a sequence of modules connected by homomorphisms,
called differentials, such that any d-fold composition of the maps is a scalar
multiple of the identity.

One can access the differential of a factorization as follows.

