dual(ZZdFactorization) -- make the dual of a ZZ/d-graded factorization
**********************************************************************

  * Function: *note dual: (Macaulay2Doc)dual,
  * Usage: 
        dual C
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note ZZ/d graded factorization: ZZdFactorization,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ZZ/d graded factorization: ZZdFactorization,, 

Description
===========

The dual of a ZZ/d-graded factorization $C$ is by definition $Hom(C, R)$, where
$R$ is the ring of $C$. If $C$ is a factorization of $f$, then the dual of $C$
is a factorization of $-f$.

+--------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ/101[a..d];          |
+--------------------------------+
|i2 : f = a^2+b^2+c^2+d^2;       |
+--------------------------------+
|i3 : R = S/(f)                  |
|                                |
|o3 = R                          |
|                                |
|o3 : QuotientRing               |
+--------------------------------+
|i4 : C1 = tailMF ideal vars R   |
|                                |
|      8      8      8           |
|o4 = S  <-- S  <-- S            |
|                                |
|     0      1      0            |
|                                |
|o4 : ZZdFactorization           |
+--------------------------------+
|i5 : C2 = dual C1               |
|                                |
|      8      8      8           |
|o5 = S  <-- S  <-- S            |
|                                |
|     0      1      0            |
|                                |
|o5 : ZZdFactorization           |
+--------------------------------+
|i6 : isdFactorization C2        |
|                                |
|               2    2    2    2 |
|o6 = (true, - a  - b  - c  - d )|
|                                |
|o6 : Sequence                   |
+--------------------------------+
