|                                |
|        2    2    2    2        |
|o8 = - a  - b  - c  - d         |
|                                |
|o8 : S                          |
+--------------------------------+

The double dual of a ZZ/2-graded factorization is isomorphic to the original
factorization. If the period of the factorization is $>2$, then one should
adjoin a root of unity to the underlying ring or factorization. This can be
done in a few different ways:

