fullCollapse -- Converts a d-fold factorization into a 2-fold factorization
***************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        fullCollapse(X, n, r)
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note ZZ/d graded factorization: ZZdFactorization,, The input
        d-fold factorization
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, Starting position for composing
        maps
      * r, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, Number of maps to compose
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ZZ/d graded factorization: ZZdFactorization,, The resulting
        2-fold factorization

Description
===========

This method converts a d-fold factorization into a 2-fold factorization by
composing the maps in the specified positions. It starts composing maps from
position n and continues composing r maps. The resulting 2-fold factorization
is returned.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : Q = ZZ/101[a,b];                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : C = linearMF(a^4+b^4, t)                                                |
|                                                                             |
|     / Q[t] \4     / Q[t] \4     / Q[t] \4     / Q[t] \4     / Q[t] \4       |
|o2 = |------|  <-- |------|  <-- |------|  <-- |------|  <-- |------|        |
|     | 2    |      | 2    |      | 2    |      | 2    |      | 2    |        |
|     \t  + 1/      \t  + 1/      \t  + 1/      \t  + 1/      \t  + 1/        |
|                                                                             |
|     0             1             2             3             0               |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : ZZdFactorization                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : C.dd                                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|         / Q[t] \4                             / Q[t] \4                     |
|o3 = 3 : |------|  <-------------------------- |------|  : 0                 |
|         | 2    |     {0, 2} | b a  0  0   |   | 2    |                      |
|         \t  + 1/     {0, 2} | 0 bt a  0   |   \t  + 1/                      |
|                      {0, 2} | 0 0  -b a   |                                 |
|                      {0, 2} | a 0  0  -bt |                                 |
|                                                                             |
|         / Q[t] \4                             / Q[t] \4                     |
|     0 : |------|  <-------------------------- |------|  : 1                 |
|         | 2    |     {0, 2} | b a  0  0   |   | 2    |                      |
