There is a simple relationship between Hom factorizations and *note shifts:
(Complexes)Complex Array,. Specifically, shifting the first argument is the
same as the negative shift of the result.  But shifting the second argument is
only the same as the positive shift of the result up to a sign.

+----------------------------+
|i18 : Hom(C[3], C) == D[-3] |
|                            |
|o18 = false                 |
+----------------------------+
|i19 : Hom(C, C[-2]) == D[-2]|
|                            |
|o19 = true                  |
+----------------------------+
|i20 : Hom(C, C[-3]) != D[-3]|
|                            |
|o20 = true                  |
+----------------------------+

Specific maps and morphisms between complexes can be obtained with the
homomorphism command.

Because the Hom factorization can be regarded as the totalization of a
d-periodic double complex, each term comes with pairs of indices, labelling the
summands.

