isdFactorization -- Checks if the differentials of a factorization compose to a scalar multiple of the identity
***************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isdFactorization(X)
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note ZZ/d graded factorization: ZZdFactorization,, The input
        d-fold matrix factorization
  * Outputs:
      * a *note sequence: (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence,, A sequence specifying
        whether the differentials of the factorization compose to a scalar
        multiple of the identity, where the second term of the sequence is the
        scalar multiple if it exists, otherwise it outputs no potential.

Description
===========

This method checks if the differentials of a factorization compose to a scalar
multiple of the identity. It returns a sequence where the first element is a
boolean value indicating whether the factorization is well-defined, and the
second element is the scalar multiple if it exists, otherwise it outputs no
potential.

This check is distinct from isWellDefined for factorizations, since it does not
do any other checks for well-definedness except for checking the differentials
compose to a scalar multiple of the identity.

