Caveat
======

This command is distinct from isWellDefined, since it only checks if the
differentials compose to be a scalar multiple of the identity.

See also
========

  * *note isWellDefined(ZZdFactorization): isWellDefined_lpZZdFactorization_rp,
    -- whether a ZZ/d-graded factorization is well-defined
  * *note tailMF(Module): tailMF, -- Generate a ZZdFactorization from a module
    over a hypersurface ring
  * *note randomTailMF(RingElement): randomTailMF, -- Construct a matrix
    factorization from a high syzygy of a random module over a hypersurface
  * *note linearMF(RingElement): linearMF, -- Constructs a Koszul d-fold
    factorization of a homogeneous element of degree d
  * *note randomLinearMF(ZZ,Ring): randomLinearMF, -- Generates a linear d-fold
    factorization of a random degree d polynomial

