isHomogeneous(ZZdFactorizationMap) -- whether a map of ZZ/d-graded factorizations is homogeneous
************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note isHomogeneous: (Macaulay2Doc)isHomogeneous,
  * Usage: 
        isHomogeneous f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note map of ZZ/d-graded factorizations: ZZdFactorizationMap,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, that is true when $f_i$
        is homogeneous, for all $i$

Description
===========

A map of factorizations $f \colon C \to D$ is homogeneous (graded) if its
underlying ring is graded, and all the component maps $f_i \colon C_i \to
D_{d+i}$ are graded of degree zero, where $f$ has degree $d$.

