linearMF -- Constructs a Koszul d-fold factorization of a homogeneous element of degree d
*****************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        linearMF(RingElement)
  * Inputs:
      * RingElement, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, A ring
        element and a Symbol of RingElement, specifying the name of a
        distinguished root of unity if one needs to be adjoined.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ZZ/d graded factorization: ZZdFactorization,, 

Description
===========

This method constructs a Koszul d-fold factorization of a homogeneous element
of degree $d$. The code first checks if the input element $f$ is homogeneous.
If it is, it constructs a Koszul d-fold factorization obtained by taking the
tensor product of the "trivial" factorizations of the constituent monomial
terms (obtained by using the *note monomialMF: monomialMF, function).

