******************************************************************************

Basic constructors
==================

  * *note map(ZZdFactorization,ZZdFactorization,HashTable):
    map_lpZZdFactorization_cmZZdFactorization_cmHashTable_rp, -- make a map of
    ZZ/d-graded factorizations
  * *note map(ZZdFactorization,ZZdFactorization,ZZ):
    map_lpZZdFactorization_cmZZdFactorization_cmZZ_rp, -- make the zero map or
    identity between ZZ/d-graded factorizations
  * *note map(ZZdFactorization,ZZdFactorization,ZZdFactorizationMap):
    map_lpZZdFactorization_cmZZdFactorization_cmZZdFactorizationMap_rp, -- make
    a new map of ZZ/d-graded factorizations from an existing one (for inducing
    maps)
  * *note id _ ZZdFactorization: id _us ZZdFactorization, -- the identity map
    of a ZZ/d-graded factorization
  * *note ZZdFactorizationMap Array: ZZdFactorization Array, -- shift a
    ZZ/d-graded factorization or map of ZZ/d-graded factorizations
  * *note isWellDefined(ZZdFactorizationMap):
    isWellDefined_lpZZdFactorizationMap_rp, -- whether a map of ZZ/d-graded
    factorizations is well-defined

Important computations creating new factorization maps
======================================================

  * *note HH ZZdFactorizationMap: HH ZZdFactorizationMap, -- induced map on
    homology or cohomology
  * *note ZZdFactorization ** Matrix: ZZdFactorization _st_st Matrix, -- create
    the tensor product of a ZZ/d-graded factorization and a map of modules
  * *note nullHomotopy(ZZdFactorizationMap):
    nullHomotopy_lpZZdFactorizationMap_rp, -- a map which is a candidate for
    being a null homotopy

Canonical maps between factorizations
=====================================

Some factorizations come with canonical maps. To access the factorization map,
one uses *note inducedMap(ZZdFactorization,ZZdFactorization):
inducedMap_lpZZdFactorization_cmZZdFactorization_rp,.

  * *note kernel(ZZdFactorizationMap): kernel_lpZZdFactorizationMap_rp, -- make
    the kernel of a map of ZZ/d-graded factorizations
  * *note cokernel(ZZdFactorizationMap): cokernel_lpZZdFactorizationMap_rp, --
    make the cokernel of a map of ZZ/d-graded factorizations
  * *note image(ZZdFactorizationMap): image_lpZZdFactorizationMap_rp, -- make
    the image of a map of ZZ/d-graded factorizations
  * *note coimage(ZZdFactorizationMap): coimage_lpZZdFactorizationMap_rp, --
    make the coimage of a map of ZZ/d-graded factorizations
  * *note cone(ZZdFactorizationMap): cone_lpZZdFactorizationMap_rp, -- make the
    mapping cone of a morphism of ZZ/d-graded factorizations
  * *note inducedMap(ZZdFactorization,ZZdFactorization):
    inducedMap_lpZZdFactorization_cmZZdFactorization_rp, -- make the map of
    ZZ/d-graded factorizations induced at each term by the identity map

Random maps of ZZ/d-graded factorizations
=========================================

The method *note randomFactorizationMap(ZZdFactorization,ZZdFactorization):
randomFactorizationMap, allows one to construct random factorization maps,
random morphisms between factorizations, and random null homotopies between
factorizations.

  * *note isCommutative(ZZdFactorizationMap):
