map(ZZdFactorization,ZZdFactorization,ZZ) -- make the zero map or identity between ZZ/d-graded factorizations
*************************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note map: (Macaulay2Doc)map,
  * Usage: 
        f = map(D, C, 0)
        f = map(C, C, 1)
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note ZZ/d graded factorization: ZZdFactorization,, 
      * D, a *note ZZ/d graded factorization: ZZdFactorization,, 
      * 0, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, or 1
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Degree: (Macaulay2Doc)map_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegree=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value null, the degree of
        the resulting map
      * *note DegreeLift: (Macaulay2Doc)map_lpRing_cmRing_cmMatrix_rp, => ...,
        default value null, unused
      * *note DegreeMap: (Macaulay2Doc)map_lpRing_cmRing_cmMatrix_rp, => ...,
        default value null, unused
  * Outputs:
      * f, a *note map of ZZ/d-graded factorizations: ZZdFactorizationMap,, the
        zero map from $C$ to $D$ or the identity map from $C$ to $C$

Description
===========

A map of ZZ/d-graded factorizations $f : C \rightarrow D$ of degree $d$ is a
sequence of maps $f_i : C_i \rightarrow D_{d+i}$.

We construct the zero map between two factorizations.

+------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ/101[a,b,c]                    |
|                                          |
|o1 = S                                    |
|                                          |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                       |
+------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R = S/(a^2+b^2+c^2);                 |
+------------------------------------------+
|i3 : m = ideal vars R                     |
|                                          |
|o3 = ideal (a, b, c)                      |
|                                          |
|o3 : Ideal of R                           |
+------------------------------------------+
|i4 : C = tailMF m                         |
|                                          |
|      4      4      4                     |
|o4 = S  <-- S  <-- S                      |
|                                          |
|     0      1      0                      |
|                                          |
|o4 : ZZdFactorization                     |
+------------------------------------------+
|i5 : D = tailMF (m^2)                     |
|                                          |
|      8      8      8                     |
|o5 = S  <-- S  <-- S                      |
|                                          |
|     0      1      0                      |
|                                          |
|o5 : ZZdFactorization                     |
+------------------------------------------+
|i6 : f = map(D, C, 0)                     |
|                                          |
|o6 = 0                                    |
|                                          |
|o6 : ZZdFactorizationMap                  |
+------------------------------------------+
|i7 : assert isWellDefined f               |
+------------------------------------------+
|i8 : assert isFactorizationMorphism f     |
+------------------------------------------+
|i9 : g = map(C, C, 0, Degree => 13)       |
|                                          |
|o9 = 0                                    |
|                                          |
|o9 : ZZdFactorizationMap                  |
+------------------------------------------+
|i10 : assert isWellDefined g              |
+------------------------------------------+
|i11 : assert(degree g == 13)              |
+------------------------------------------+
|i12 : assert not isFactorizationMorphism g|
+------------------------------------------+
|i13 : assert isCommutative g              |
+------------------------------------------+
|i14 : assert isHomogeneous g              |
+------------------------------------------+
|i15 : assert(source g == C)               |
+------------------------------------------+
|i16 : assert(target g == C)               |
+------------------------------------------+

Using this function to create the identity map is the same as using *note id _
ZZdFactorization: id _us ZZdFactorization,.

+-----------------------------------+
|i17 : assert(map(C, C, 1) === id_C)|
+-----------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note ZZdFactorizationMap: ZZdFactorizationMap, -- the class of all maps
    between ZZ/d-graded factorizations
  * *note isWellDefined(ZZdFactorizationMap):
    isWellDefined_lpZZdFactorizationMap_rp, -- whether a map of ZZ/d-graded
    factorizations is well-defined
  * *note degree(ZZdFactorizationMap): degree_lpZZdFactorizationMap_rp, -- get
    the degree of a map of ZZ/d-graded factorizations
  * *note isCommutative(ZZdFactorizationMap):
    isCommutative_lpZZdFactorizationMap_rp, -- whether a ZZ/d-graded
    factorization map commutes with the differentials
  * *note source(ZZdFactorizationMap): source_lpZZdFactorizationMap_rp, -- get
    the source of a map of ZZ/d-graded factorizations
  * *note target(ZZdFactorizationMap): target_lpZZdFactorizationMap_rp, -- get
    the target of a map of ZZ/d-graded factorizations
  * *note id _ ZZdFactorization: id _us ZZdFactorization, -- the identity map
    of a ZZ/d-graded factorization

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note map(ZZdFactorization,ZZdFactorization,ZZ):
    map_lpZZdFactorization_cmZZdFactorization_cmZZ_rp, -- make the zero map or
    identity between ZZ/d-graded factorizations
