tailMF -- Generate a ZZdFactorization from a module over a hypersurface ring
****************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        tailMF(Module)
  * Inputs:
      * Module, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, A module over a
        hypersurface ring or an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal, in a
        hypersurface ring
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ZZ/d graded factorization: ZZdFactorization,, 

Description
===========

The function tailMF takes a module $M$ over a hypersurface ring $R = S/(f)$ and
generates a ZZdFactorization. This involves computing a resolution of $M$ over
the hypersurface $R$, taking a high truncation of this resolution, lifting it
to the ambient ring $S$, then finding a null homotopy for multiplication by
$f$.

