unfold -- Converts a factorization into a complex
*************************************************

  * Usage: 
        unfold(ZZdFactorization, L)
        unfold(ZZdFactorization, d)
  * Inputs:
      * ZZdFactorization, a *note ZZ/d graded factorization: ZZdFactorization,,
        A ZZdFactorization
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, A list specifying the endpoint
        homological degrees
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, An integer representing the
        endpoint homological degree
  * Outputs:
      * a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, 

Description
===========

Converts a factorization into a complex, where the list specifies the endpoint
homological degrees. This method converts a factorization into a complex by
specifying the homological degrees. If a single integer is provided, it takes
homological endpoints from degrees 0 to d.

+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ/101[a..c];                                  |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : C = koszulMF(a^3+b^3+c^3)                          |
|                                                        |
|      4      4      4                                   |
|o2 = S  <-- S  <-- S                                    |
|                                                        |
|     0      1      0                                    |
|                                                        |
|o2 : ZZdFactorization                                   |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : E = Hom(C,C)                                       |
|                                                        |
|      32      32      32                                |
|o3 = S   <-- S   <-- S                                  |
|                                                        |
|     0       1       0                                  |
|                                                        |
|o3 : ZZdFactorization                                   |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : Eu = unfold(E, {-3,3})                             |
|                                                        |
|      32      32      32      32      32      32      32|
|o4 = S   <-- S   <-- S   <-- S   <-- S   <-- S   <-- S  |
|                                                        |
|     -3      -2      -1      0       1       2       3  |
|                                                        |
|o4 : Complex                                            |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : isWellDefined Eu                                   |
|                                                        |
|o5 = true                                               |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : concentration Eu                                   |
|                                                        |
|o6 = (-3, 3)                                            |
|                                                        |
|o6 : Sequence                                           |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : prune HH_0 Eu == prune HH_0 E                      |
|                                                        |
|o7 = true                                               |
+--------------------------------------------------------+

If only one integer is specified, then the start point of the unfolded object
is assumed to be homological degree 0. Beware as well that unfolding a
factorization of a nonzero polynomial is not a well-defined complex.

+-----------------------------------+
|i8 : unfold(E, 3)                  |
|                                   |
|      32      32      32      32   |
|o8 = S   <-- S   <-- S   <-- S     |
|                                   |
|     0       1       2       3     |
|                                   |
|o8 : Complex                       |
+-----------------------------------+
|i9 : Cu = unfold(C, 4)             |
|                                   |
|      4      4      4      4      4|
|o9 = S  <-- S  <-- S  <-- S  <-- S |
|                                   |
|     0      1      2      3      4 |
|                                   |
|o9 : Complex                       |
+-----------------------------------+
|i10 : assert not isWellDefined Cu  |
+-----------------------------------+

The *note Fold: Fold, and unfold functors are not inverses to each other and
will in general change the homology of a ZZ/d-graded complex.

+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : E' = Fold(unfold(E,1), 2)                                      |
|                                                                     |
|       32      32      32                                            |
|o11 = S   <-- S   <-- S                                              |
|                                                                     |
|      0       1       0                                              |
|                                                                     |
|o11 : ZZdFactorization                                               |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : E'.dd_1 == E.dd_1                                              |
|                                                                     |
|o12 = true                                                           |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : E'.dd_0 --the information of the 0th differential has been lost|
|                                                                     |
|o13 = 0                                                              |
|                                                                     |
|              32      32                                             |
|o13 : Matrix S   <-- S                                               |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : Fold(unfold(E,2), 2)                                           |
|                                                                     |
|       64      32      64                                            |
|o14 = S   <-- S   <-- S                                              |
|                                                                     |
|      0       1       0                                              |
|                                                                     |
|o14 : ZZdFactorization                                               |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+

This method is also functorial, applying to factorization maps with the same
syntax.

