ZZdFactorization _ Array -- the canonical inclusion or projection map of a direct sum
*************************************************************************************

  * Operator: *note _: (Macaulay2Doc)_us,
  * Usage: 
        i = C_[name]
        p = C^[name]
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note ZZ/d graded factorization: ZZdFactorization,, 
      * name, an *note array: (Macaulay2Doc)Array,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note map of ZZ/d-graded factorizations: ZZdFactorizationMap,, i is
        the canonical inclusion and p is the canonical projection

Description
===========

The direct sum is an n-ary operator with projection and inclusion maps from
each component satisfying appropriate identities.

One can access these maps as follows.

+----------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ/101[a,b,c];                 |
+----------------------------------------+
|i2 : f = a^3+b^3+c^3;                   |
+----------------------------------------+
|i3 : C1 = randomTailMF(f, 2, 4, 4)      |
|                                        |
|      4      4      4                   |
|o3 = S  <-- S  <-- S                    |
|                                        |
|     0      1      0                    |
|                                        |
|o3 : ZZdFactorization                   |
+----------------------------------------+
|i4 : C2 = randomTailMF(f, 2, 4, 4)      |
|                                        |
|      4      4      4                   |
|o4 = S  <-- S  <-- S                    |
|                                        |
|     0      1      0                    |
|                                        |
|o4 : ZZdFactorization                   |
+----------------------------------------+
|i5 : D = C1 ++ C2                       |
|                                        |
|      8      8      8                   |
|o5 = S  <-- S  <-- S                    |
|                                        |
|     0      1      0                    |
|                                        |
|o5 : ZZdFactorization                   |
+----------------------------------------+
|i6 : isdFactorization D                 |
|                                        |
|             3    3    3                |
|o6 = (true, a  + b  + c )               |
|                                        |
|o6 : Sequence                           |
+----------------------------------------+
|i7 : D_[0]                              |
|                                        |
|          8                       4     |
|o7 = 0 : S  <------------------- S  : 0 |
|               {3} | 1 0 0 0 |          |
