ZZdFactorization _ ZZ -- access individual object in a ZZ/d-graded factorization
********************************************************************************

  * Operator: *note _: (Macaulay2Doc)_us,
  * Usage: 
        C_i
        C^i
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note ZZ/d graded factorization: ZZdFactorization,, 
      * i, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, either the homological or
        cohomological index
  * Outputs:
      * a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, the i-th object

Description
===========

ZZ/d-graded factorizations can be either homologically or cohomologically
graded.  Subscripts refer to homological indices, and superscripts refer to
cohomological indices.

In this package homological indices are used by default.  We always have the
equation $C^i = C_{-i}$.

+---------------------------------------------------+
