ZZdFactorizationMap == ZZdFactorizationMap -- whether two ZZ/d-graded factorization maps are equal
**************************************************************************************************

  * Operator: *note ==: (Macaulay2Doc)==,
  * Usage: 
        f == g
        f == 0
        f == 1
        f == r
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note map of ZZ/d-graded factorizations: ZZdFactorizationMap,, or
        0, or 1.
      * g, a *note map of ZZ/d-graded factorizations: ZZdFactorizationMap,, or
        0, or 1, or any RingElement.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, that is true when f and
        g are equal, or when f is equal to the 0 map, the identity map, or a
        scalar multiple of the identity map.

Description
===========

Two ZZ/d-graded factorization maps are equal if they have the same source, the
same target, and $f_i = g_i$ for all $i$.

