ZZdFactorizationMap ^ Array -- the composition with the canonical inclusion or projection map
*********************************************************************************************

  * Operator: *note ^: (Macaulay2Doc)^,
  * Usage: 
        i = f_[name]
        p = f^[name]
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note map of ZZ/d-graded factorizations: ZZdFactorizationMap,, 
      * name, an *note array: (Macaulay2Doc)Array,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note map of ZZ/d-graded factorizations: ZZdFactorizationMap,, i is
        the composition of f with the canonical inclusion and p is the
        composition of the canonical projection with f

Description
===========

The direct sum is an n-ary operator with projection and inclusion maps from
each component satisfying appropriate identities.

One can access these maps as follows.  First, we define some non-trivial maps
of chain complexes.

