ZZdFactorizationMap ^ ZZ -- the n-fold composition
**************************************************

  * Operator: *note ^: (Macaulay2Doc)^,
  * Usage: 
        f^n
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note map of ZZ/d-graded factorizations: ZZdFactorizationMap,,
        whose source and target are the same ZZ/d-graded factorization
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note map of ZZ/d-graded factorizations: ZZdFactorizationMap,, the
        composition of $f$ with itself $n$ times.

Description
===========

A ZZ/d-graded factorization map $f : C \to C$ can be composed with itself. This
method produces these new maps of ZZ/d-graded factorizations.

The differential on a ZZ/d-graded factorization should compose with itself d
times to give a scalar multiple of the identity map.

